# every file somebody touched, which store files the pointer NAMED for it — not "a session opened
# this", but "at the moment of the work, this rule governs it". Measured the day it was first read,
# over 241 records: 27 for `the-set-not-the-member.md`, 10 for the round-numbering rule, 5 for
# extend-a-skill. The most-governing rule was the one nobody could read.
#
